# ── Source footage and anything derived from it ───────────────────────────
# These are recordings of real people, several of them victims of the crimes
# being detected. Frames, snapshots and mined negatives are all identifiable
# imagery. None of it belongs in a code repository, whatever its visibility.
videos/
logs/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
!frontend/public/**

# ── Datasets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every image dataset under here is either derived from the source footage,
# redistributed from a third party (Sohas is CC BY-SA and 1.8 GB), or both.
# The label files are excluded alongside the images: on their own they are
# thousands of files that reference pictures nobody else has.
#
# What IS tracked is the annotation CSVs — the human labelling work, which is
# small, hand-made, and the part that would actually hurt to lose.
training/data/weapons/
training/data/**/images/
training/data/**/labels/
!training/data/*.csv

# Archives: GitHub rejects anything over 100 MB and training/archive.zip is
# 217 MB, which fails the push rather than warning about it.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.npz

# ── Model weights ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Large, reproducible from the training scripts, and in the case of the
# public weapon checkpoint, not ours to redistribute.
checkpoints/
*.onnx
*.pt
*.pth
model_export/

# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.env

# ── Node ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
frontend/.env*.local

# ── OS / editor ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp

# Gradio runtime cache (vendored LLaVA demo)
.gradio/
